   About us:\
\
Our Story: \
\
Founding Vision: Our founder, Dylan Harris, lives and breathes art. Not just in the traditional sense but in all forms whether it is, paintings, drawings, or music. Art is all around us but here at Dylan\'92s Gallery we create art that you can carry with you for a lifetime. Your body is our canvas. We started off as a mobile service doing house calls but over the years we have developed and grown thanks to our artists and clients and our hope is that through all of you we can continue bringing art into our communities 1 tattoo at time. \
\
Our philosophy: There is nothing too crazy, or weird for us. Here at Dylan\'92s Gallery our sole purpose is to bring your vision to life. That is why we do custom tattoo designs based on what you bring us. Our artists specialise in any style you can think of so don\'92t worry about a thing. Client experience is a priority for us so you can expect a comfortable, safe and creative environment when you come to our parlour. You are in safe hands here at Dylan\'92s Gallery.\
\
Our Vision: To encourage you to express who you are through artworks that you love and carry with you forever. \
\
How things work? You can book a consultation by filling in the form on our Contact us page. You will then receive confirmation about your consultation date and time and you will be contacted via WhatsApp to send through your design ideas. The artist you chose will work with you in creating exactly what you want. Then you will be able to come through to the parlour where you will be greeted by one of our team members. You will then be shown to our waiting area where you can browse through some of our design books, take in the artworks on the wall or enjoy the sick music playlist put together by Cayd Symons who is one of our artists. This is so we can prep the work station. All that is left is for you to get your tattoo/s!!! \
\
Health and safety \
\
Sterilisation protocols are hospital standard to ensure your safety and well-being. We use single-use needles and equipment which are disposed of after each session. Any reusable tools are sterilised in medical-grade fashion while all surfaces and work stations are disinfected between each client. We only have the best artists. All are well-trained, certified and licensed. Our staff regularly go through health and safety seminars to ensure the best and safest environment for all our clients. We use only high quality, non-toxic ink sourced from well respected suppliers. We do ask clients to ensure they don\'92t have any allergies pertaining to the ink and if they are not sure we offer patch tests. You can find out more about Aftercare under our FAQ\'92s page. \
\
