FAQ\
\
Does getting a tattoo hurt ?\
The answer varies from person to person. It also depends on where you are getting the tattoo on your body and the size of it. Everyone\'92s pain tolerance is different so the answer is you won\'92t know until you try!\
\
How do I choose the right design?\
We have a very experienced group of artists who can assist you with this but the important thing is that you choose a design that speaks to you and think about things like the size of the tattoo, the location of the tattoo and how it makes you feel.\
\
How do I prepare for my tattoo appointment? \
Make sure you get enough sleep, have something you eat before you embark on the experience. Avoid alcohol a day before and after getting your tattoo and don\'92t overthink it!\
\
What is the aftercare process like? \
We go through this with you after getting your tattoo to make sure you fully understand. But keep the wrapping on for 3-4 hours after getting your tattoo. Avoid direct sunlight. Clean your tattoo with fragrance free soap, dap it, don\'92t wipe. Was twice a day and we recommend using Epi Max Baby Lotion after each wash. Do this for about 2-3 weeks. Try to avoid getting the tattoo wet apart from when you are cleaning and do not pick at the scabs, let them fall off naturally. \
\
How much does it cost?\
That depends on size and complexity and things like whether you would like coloured ink but don\'92t worry you will get a clear breakdown of the price after you work with one of our artists on your design.\
\
Can I get a tattoo if I am pregnant or breastfeeding?\
It Is advised that you wait until after pregnancy and breastfeeding. \
\
What should I not do before my appointment? \
Avoid caffeine, alcohol or any blood thinning medication.\
\
How do I book an appointment? \
You fill out the form on our contact us page, you will then be contacted by the artist you chose to send through your design, thereafter you will receive an email with your appointment information.\
